* Fischer vs. [[Mark Taimanov]], Vancouver Candidates Final 1971; 4th match game, [[Sicilian Defense]], [[Sicilian Defence#Taimanov Variation|Taimanov Variation]] (B47), {{chessAN|1–0}}.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.chessgames.com/perl/chessgame?gid=1044361 |title=Robert James Fischer vs. Mark Taimanov, Candidates Quarterfinal, Vancouver 1971 |website=[[Chessgames.com]] }}</ref> Fischer's patient and accurate handling of bishop vs. knight, first in the rook and minor piece [[Chess endgame|endgame]], and then after rooks were {{chessgloss|exchanged}}, has become a staple of endgame instructional literature.<ref>{{cite magazine |author=Danny Kopec |author2=Daniel Kostovetsky |name-list-style=amp |date=March 2014 |title=The Fischer Ending |magazine=Chess Life |pages=39–43 }}</ref>{{parabr}}
